    "title": "US Coast Guard Can Shift to Tsunami Readiness at Relatively Quick Speed: Retired Lieutenant Commander | NTD",
    "text": "U.S. shores, including in Hawaii, California, Oregon, Washington, and Alaska, have been hit by waves. The tsunami’s first waves hit Russia and Japan. For analysis on this, NTD spoke to Steven Rogers, a retired Lieutenant Commander who served in the Office of Naval Intelligence. He’s also a retired New Jersey Police Detective and former member of the FBI National Joint Terrorism Task Force.\nUS Coast Guard Can Shift to Tsunami Readiness at Relatively Quick Speed: Retired Lieutenant Commander\nRetired Lt Cdr. Steven Rogers discussed the US Coast Guard's readiness levels when responding to a tsunami.\nBy\n|\nPublished: 7/30/2025, 11:14:26 PM EDT",
